What to do next

firefox: Notes 1.4.0 passed validation.

  1. Submit the add-on's first version on the site, uploading the package and its source.
     Open   https://addons.mozilla.org/developers/addon/submit/distribution
     Package: firefox.zip
     Source code: firefox-source.zip
     Build instructions: BUILD.md, inside the source archive
     Why by hand: the API publishes versions of an add-on that exists; creating one asks for a license and categories
     Done when: `leptoskit publish firefox --submit` creates versions instead

  2. Choose the add-on's license on that page. (you, the account holder)
     Why by hand: a license is a legal choice for the account holder
     Done when: the first submission is done

  3. Add the listing's privacy policy.
     Open   https://addons.mozilla.org/developers/addon/notes@example.com/edit
     Privacy policy: (add privacy_policy to store/listing.toml)
     Screenshots: (add the chrome-1280x800 size to store/screenshots/screenshots.toml, and run `leptoskit publish screenshots`; each upload sends them)
     Summary: (write it in store/en-US/summary.md, 250 characters at most)
     Description: (write it in store/en-US/description.md)
     Why by hand: leptoskit uploads the name, summary, description, and screenshots with each upload, but the API doesn't set the privacy policy
     Done when: the listing page shows it

  4. Decide to release it, then run `leptoskit publish firefox --submit`. (you, the account holder)
     Why by hand: a listed version goes to review and then to users
     Done when: addons.mozilla.org shows the version awaiting review
